{"id":"cmpl-4410e2c561ba46c995a0637e36411910","object":"text_completion","created":1744664714,"model":"./models/qwen72b","choices":[{"index":0,"text":" city in, and the county of, San Francisco in the U.S. state of California. Founded on June 29, 1776, it is the cultural, commercial, and financial center of Northern California. San Francisco is the 13th-most populous city in the United States, and the fourth-most populous in California, with 883,305 residents as of 2019. It covers an area of about , mostly at the north end of the San Francisco Peninsula in the San Francisco Bay Area, making it the second-most densely populated large U.S. city, and the fifth-most densely populated U.S. county, behind only four of the five New York City boroughs. San Francisco is also part of the fifth-most populous primary statistical area in the United States, the San Jose–San Francisco–Oakland, CA Combined Statistical Area (9.7 million residents as of 2018). As of 2019, it was the seventh-highest income county in the United States, with a per capita personal income of $119,868. As of 2019, San Francisco was ranked high on world livability rankings.\nSan Francisco is home to several educational and cultural institutions such as the University of San Francisco (USF), University of California, San Francisco (UCSF), San Francisco State University (SFSU), the de Young Museum, the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art, the San Francisco Ballet, and the Academy of Art University. It hosts numerous annual events, including the Bay to Breakers foot race, the Outside Lands Music Festival, the Folsom Street Fair, the San Francisco Film Festival, the Hardly Strictly Bluegrass Festival, and the Pride Parade. It is well known for its cool summers, fog, steep rolling hills, eclectic mix of architecture, and landmarks, including the Golden Gate Bridge, cable cars, the former Alcatraz Federal Penitentiary, Fisherman's Wharf, and its Chinatown district. Its diverse population gives the city a cosmopolitan feel, along with its status as a world-renowned travel destination and as one of the top tourist destinations in the state of California.\nSan Francisco is a popular tourist destination, ranking as the 24th most visited city in the world, and second-most visited city in the United States as of 2017. The city is also known for its restaurants, with the most Michelin stars of any city in North America, and its haute cuisine and foodie culture. San Francisco is the headquarters of five major banking institutions and various other companies such as Reddit, Square, Inc., Airbnb, Weebly, Pacific Gas and Electric Company, Yelp, Pinterest, Twitter, Uber, Lyft, and the headquarters of five major financial institutions. It has been a hotbed of innovation and entrepreneurship from the dot-com boom of the late 1990s to the social media boom of the mid-2000s up to the present day. The city is also home to the San Francisco 49ers of the National Football League (NFL) and the San Francisco Giants of Major League Baseball (MLB).\nThe earliest archaeological evidence of human habitation of the territory of the city of San Francisco dates to 3000 BC. The Yelamu group of the Ohlone people resided in a number of villages around the San Francisco Bay.\nA Spanish exploration party, led by Don Gaspar de Portolà, reached the area of what today is San Francisco on November 2, 1769. Seven years later, on March 28, 1776, the Presidio of San Francisco was established by colonists from New Spain. On September 17, 1776, the Mission San Francisco de Asís was founded by Spanish missionaries and is the oldest building in San Francisco. Mission San Francisco de Asís was later named Mission Dolores after a nearby stream. The Mission became the basis of the Spanish colony that would later become San Francisco; Mission Dolores is still open to public worship at 16th and Dolores Streets. Until the 1800s, the Yelamu remained in the area of Mission Dolores.\nUpon independence from Spain in 1821, the area became part of Mexico. Under Mexican rule, the mission system gradually ended and many of its lands became privatized. In 1835, Englishman William Richardson erected the first significant homestead outside Mission Dolores, near the present-day intersection of Geary Boulevard and Larkin Street. Together with Alcalde Francisco de Haro, he laid out a street plan for the expanded settlement and claimed homestead rights to the land outside the mission settlement. This configuration gave rise to today's downtown street grid.\nYerba Buena","logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"length","stop_reason":null,"prompt_logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":4,"total_tokens":1004,"completion_tokens":1000,"prompt_tokens_details":null}}

